# Afenda core architecture

Canonical doctrine: `docs/architecture/` (**ARCH-1001**–**ARCH-1006**). Index: `docs/architecture/README.md`.

**Target-only:** Deviations from ARCH are **non-compliant**, not legacy OK. Agent discipline: `.cursor/rules/afenda-agent-discipline.mdc`. Hook: `guard-architecture-compliance.mjs` (`failClosed`).

**Authority when docs conflict:** ARCH-1002 (feature packages) → ARCH-1001 (runtime) → update the other doc in the same PR. **ARCH-1005** — monorepo guards (`pnpm architecture:check`).

## Layout

- `apps/erp` — only deployable Next.js app (`@afenda/erp`).
- `packages/*` — workspace libraries; `@afenda/feature-*` under `packages/features/<moduleId>` (flat workspaces, grouped `src/` internals).
- No nested `packages/features/<moduleId>/<category>/package.json` unless ARCH-1005 and the guard script are updated together.
- No `apps/erp/src/components/ui/` — primitives live in `@afenda/ui`.
- Library packages emit `dist/**`; app emits `.next/**` (exclude `.next/cache/**` from Turborepo cache).

## Imports

| From | May import |
| ---- | ---------- |
| `apps/erp` | Public doors only: `@afenda/feature-*` (`.`, `./client`, `./server`, `./metadata`), `@afenda/kernel`, platform packages — never `/src`, `/dist`, or `/internal` |
| `@afenda/feature-*` | domain, db, auth, governed-surface, ui, workflows, observability — **not** `apps/erp` |
| `@afenda/ui` | Primitives only — no db, auth server, AI, or governed metadata |

Required feature export doors: `.`, `./client`, `./server`, `./metadata` (`default` → compiled `./dist/*.js`). `./client` must not import `@afenda/db`, `@afenda/ai`, `@afenda/workflows`, `@afenda/auth/server`, or `node:*`. New app workspace deps must appear in `afendaTranspilePackages` (`packages/config/src/next.ts`).

## Tenancy and security

- Resolve org from server session; never use client `organizationId` as source of truth.
- Enforce capabilities at mutation and sensitive read boundaries, not only in navigation/proxy.
- Validate boundaries with Zod (forms, query params, webhooks, AI structured output).

## Verification

Run `pnpm architecture:check` on layout/export/doc changes. Run `pnpm lint:governed-renderers` when touching governed renderers or registry. Schema changes: `packages/db/src/schema` → `pnpm db:generate` → `pnpm db:migrate` (rule `afenda-database-migrations` — no hand-written migration SQL unless the user explicitly requires it).

Repo root: test output under `.artifacts/` only; never root `artifacts/`, `build-log.txt`, or MCP snapshot dumps (rule `afenda-repo-hygiene`).
